{"title":"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Variation_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Variation of Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349097a0033d438020f14d96381b189edc30c186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\,$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> for which\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6dfef2630f9d364c3d85c8652f289df5a017f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor\\log_2{1}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\log_2{2}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\log_2{3}\\rfloor+\\cdots+\\lfloor\\log_2{n}\\rfloor=1994\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"19\" />\n(For real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82abef56929c38f0bf8011a2e394189e76f871e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\,$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a9d21a7fa717c0d0b69b58a8937ccf34b5cdd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c4f748b5fcef16dccd65046b4471fe6393e6b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le x.\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b5b161fea63e6a961cc3f6f52324161ea0a516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x \\le a&lt;2^{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e1fc2610d0ab9747b552684df1356df224e62a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/face6cef68f40c8b969931c368e981ca4dd24c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{a}\\rfloor=\\log_2{2^{x}}=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/674388bec538207d0fd009218db5aee3b60389ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{x+1}-2^{x}=2^{x}$\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520333286ae1b1d88911d965fcb48cb2358062a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{a}\\rfloor=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" />. So the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680c77c76f42b509d0e2403d8c9b39f940333ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{a}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> for all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40568c4a362cad3b0704376cc23b3dbab91b4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\cdot2^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0967b01b0880453373e168a27abfc6cc6e61b926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k \\le n&lt;2^{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. So for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8e96ed92da64249f9b7d78bb5b5b46c3073f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58da83b2af6a8b4d6fe176919320e5a5bbeca596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^j$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372421be27cf47bbeec8eb1a2c2b0f4d44f49748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07ae4a37b335d7e471b3d257a5578df7c83a933c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{a}\\rfloor=j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"19\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48e5f837bfa25bdc0b9f629769327271f29ca34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-2^k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" /> such integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62a060eee2cdd109eea77be959fe56486736f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{a}\\rfloor=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e205683ea0d7bc0bbfe5b656b56e3460a2a33643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_2{1}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\log_2{2}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\log_2{3}\\rfloor+\\cdots+\\lfloor\\log_2{n}\\rfloor= \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}(j\\cdot2^j) + k(n-2^k+1) = 1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"639\" height=\"53\" />. \n</p><p>Through computation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf5b568650056c34df7fe1b6ba52f1b7e0c40b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=0}^{7}(j\\cdot2^j)=1538&lt;1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"198\" height=\"52\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73536e4ac62a9496e18f1309081e7c2fe8ba621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=0}^{8}(j\\cdot2^j)=3586&gt;1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"198\" height=\"52\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77eb455e13266e46765af4d7b5506c4e3a6b314d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04daebb6a660ab67875d81fbca5cbb1003f3f80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}(j\\cdot2^j) + k(n-2^k+1) = 1538+8(n-2^8+1)=1994 \\Rightarrow n = \\boxed{312}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"555\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, one could notice this is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetico-geometric_series\" title=\"Arithmetico-geometric series\">arithmetico-geometric series</a> and avoid a lot of computation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For this solution, we notice that values between ranges of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> are the same. Let's look at these ranges and their total value. It is trivial to conclude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3dff8eac17f84650a2d18c27bf98ad2116a5729a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{1} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> so we will not write that.\n</p><p>\\begin{array}{c|c}\n\\text{Range of } k &amp; \\text{Expression (Total)} \\\\\n\\hline\n2 \\leq k &lt; 2^2 &amp; 1 \\cdot (2^2 - 2) = 2 \\\\\n2^2 \\leq k &lt; 2^3 &amp; 2 \\cdot (2^3 - 2^2) = 8 \\\\\n2^3 \\leq k &lt; 2^4 &amp; 3 \\cdot (2^4 - 2^3) = 24 \\\\\n2^4 \\leq k &lt; 2^5 &amp; 4 \\cdot (2^5 - 2^4) = 64 \\\\\n2^5 \\leq k &lt; 2^6 &amp; 5 \\cdot (2^6 - 2^5) = 160 \\\\\n2^6 \\leq k &lt; 2^7 &amp; 6 \\cdot (2^7 - 2^6) = 384 \\\\\n2^7 \\leq k &lt; 2^8 &amp; 7 \\cdot (2^8 - 2^7) = 896 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n</p><p>Sum of the values up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94dea1c5571d22db061c4607f8b70f6330bcdf10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1538$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. This seems close enough to our desired value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b6fb7a1d8b2bd77671950bb223396c2c43af6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> as any additional groups would exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b6fb7a1d8b2bd77671950bb223396c2c43af6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. The difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abdb82b4e7815d66d697250e510097fc10e17e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1996 - 1538 = 456$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />. Since the next numbers of the sequence will always be 8 since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a5530274273d82641a906f7bb658eccca4f1fc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_2{2^8 + n &lt; 2^9} \\rfloor = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" />, we can just find the number of '8's, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0a0467ac62900e4c0503e4bacdb137a9da12db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{456}{8} = 57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />. So there are exactly 57 integers in that range. The largest integer, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e55b801ed5235c85e4cd2ead5333175ee748031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8 + 56 = \\boxed{312}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"122\" height=\"25\" />. ~Totient4Breakfast\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Variation_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Variation_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 3 (Variation of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Variation of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, continue upon realization that we get the series \\( 0 + 2(1) + 4(2) + 8(3) + \\dots + k(n) \\).\n</p><p>Then, this series can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e79fb308376c83279f34ede3caabc39afbed41d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^n k2^k = 1994\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"48\" />\nContinuing forth with solution 1, we can see that if \\( n=7 \\), we get \\( 1538 &lt; 1994 \\), and if \\( n=8 \\), we get \\( 3586 &gt; 1994 \\).\n</p><p>Then, we see that there must be \\( m(8) \\) such that \\( 1538 + 8m = 1994 \\). Solving for \\( m \\) we get \\( m=57 \\).\n</p><p>We see that \\( 2^k + 2^{k+1} + 2^{k+2} + \\dots + 2^{k+n} \\) is the number of terms in this sequence for \\( 0 \\le k \\le 7 \\) and \\( n=7 \\), and we include the additional 57 terms. To do this, we don't want to include the arithmetic portion of our series, turning our arithmetico-geometric series into\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e740e5837c3c02c2ad3c8c7a88a2e250ef8e5377.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^n 2^k\\right) + 57\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"53\" />\nThe finite geometric sum results in 255, in which the value of \\( n \\) is determined as \\( 255 + 57 = \\)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade1746cfb81a064e679b90ec858f103e8ff0d80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{312}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME\" title=\"1994 AIME\">1994 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1994 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1994\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- 